"},"version":"1.0.4","_npmUser":{"name":"marijn","email":"marijn@haverbeke.berlin"},"homepage":"https://code.haverbeke.berlin/marijn/find-cluster-break","keywords":["unicode","grapheme","cluster","break"],"repository":{"url":"git+https://code.haverbeke.berlin/marijn/find-cluster-break.git","type":"git"},"_npmVersion":"11.9.0","description":"Find the position of grapheme cluster breaks in a string","directories":{},"maintainers":[{"name":"marijn","email":"marijn@haverbeke.berlin"}],"_nodeVersion":"22.20.0","_hasShrinkwrap":false,"devDependencies":{"mocha":"^10.7.3","rollup":"^4.28.1"},"_npmOperationalInternal":{"host":"s3://npm-registry-packages-npm-production","tmp":"tmp/find-cluster-break_1.0.4_1787309772967_0.333958621640559"}}},"time":{"created":"2024-10-06T18:44:20.701Z","modified":"2026-08-21T10:56:13.228Z","1.0.0":"2024-10-06T18:44:21.031Z","1.0.1":"2024-12-09T15:40:09.949Z","1.0.2":"2024-12-09T16:15:31.824Z","1.0.3":"2026-06-27T10:38:20.193Z","1.0.4":"2026-08-21T10:56:13.060Z"},"bugs":{"url":"https://code.haverbeke.berlin/marijn/find-cluster-break/issues"},"author":{"name":"Marijn Haverbeke","email":"marijn@haverbeke.berlin"},"license":"MIT","homepage":"https://code.haverbeke.berlin/marijn/find-cluster-break","keywords":["unicode","grapheme","cluster","break"],"repository":{"url":"git+https://code.haverbeke.berlin/marijn/find-cluster-break.git","type":"git"},"description":"Find the position of grapheme cluster breaks in a string","maintainers":[{"name":"marijn","email":"marijn@haverbeke.berlin"}],"readme":"# @marijn/find-cluster-break\n\nSmall JavaScript module for finding grapheme cluster breaks in\nstrings, scanning from a given position.\n\n```javascript\nimport {findClusterBreak} from \"@marijn/find-cluster-break\"\nconsole.log(findClusterBreak(\"💪🏽🦋\", 0))\n// → 4\n```\n\nThis code is open source, released under an MIT license.\n    \n## Documentation\n\n**`findClusterBreak`**`(str: string, pos: number, forward = true, includeExtending = true): number`\n\nReturns a next grapheme cluster break _after_ (not equal to) `pos`,\nif `forward` is true, or before otherwise. Returns `pos` itself if no\nfurther cluster break is available in the string. Moves across\nsurrogate pairs, extending characters (when `includeExtending` is\ntrue, which is the default), characters joined with zero-width joiners,\nand flag emoji.\n\n**`isExtendingChar`**`(code: number): boolean`\n\nQuery whether the given character has a `Grapheme_Cluster_Break` value\nof `Extend` in Unicode.\n","readmeFilename":"README.md"}